        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124">

                <pb facs="0316" n="192" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg192"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862T.01/561½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of State of a Conversation
                        with the German Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wiedfeldt</hi>),
                        <hi rendition="#italic">January 23, 1923</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1923-01-23">January 23,
                        1923</date>
                </dateline>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <p>The German Ambassador said that in view of the departure of the American forces
                    from Germany today his Government had <pb facs="0317" n="193" xml:id="pg193"/>
                    instructed him to express to the Secretary the sincere thanks of the German
                    Government for the correct conduct of the American troops during the time of
                    occupation.</p>
            </div>
